  "substitutions": [
    "Synthetic provider/cache callbacks, transparent response/request value-copy interfaces and case-insensitive standard header-map lookup.",
    "Inert std::error_code category identity and wrapper storage preserve the original chosen error integer.",
    "Original libc memory/strings/domain matcher/status getters and decision routine instructions execute unchanged; standard allocation/weak locks are inherited providers.",
    "Synthetic standard function destruction and live shared-owner reference counts permit no-callback paths to return normally.",
    "Next-request headers execute original request decorators with explicit cached/replacement token sentinels, modeling completed provider renewal, not proving its implementation.",
    "Synthetic response URL field is an explicit input; its producer and response-chain order need separate original binding proof."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Native callback decisions and next-request credential fields only; acquisition, transport dispatch, response construction and live server admission are not inferred.",
    "Chain order is supplied by the separate native-http-response-chain evidence; only original success callbacks advance to the next decorator.",
    "Capture stops at each resulting forwarding/error callback; cleanup is executed only for paths returning without either callback.",
    "All inputs are synthetic and no account/profile/process/network is used."
  ],
